**Creating Optional:**

```java
// of: wraps non-null value (THROWS NPE if null!)
Optional<Trade> trade = Optional.of(trade1);          // OK
// Optional.of(null);                                  //  NullPointerException!

// ofNullable: wraps potentially null value (null → empty)
Optional<Trade> maybeTrade = Optional.ofNullable(findTrade("TRD-999"));  // empty if null

// empty: explicit absence
Optional<Trade> absent = Optional.empty();
```

**Consuming Optional (the safe way):**

```java
// orElse: default value (always evaluated)
Trade result = maybeTrade.orElse(defaultTrade);

// orElseGet: lazy default (Supplier — only called if empty)
Trade result = maybeTrade.orElseGet(() -> createDefaultTrade());

// orElseThrow: throw if empty
Trade result = maybeTrade.orElseThrow(() -> new TradeNotFoundException("TRD-999"));

// ifPresent: action only if present
maybeTrade.ifPresent(t -> log.info("Found: {}", t.getTradeId()));

// ifPresentOrElse (Java 9):
maybeTrade.ifPresentOrElse(
    t -> log.info("Found: {}", t),
    () -> log.warn("Trade not found")
);

// map: transform if present, empty if absent
Optional<String> symbol = maybeTrade.map(Trade::getSymbol);  // Optional<String>

// flatMap: for nested Optionals
Optional<String> note = maybeTrade.flatMap(Trade::getRiskNote);  // if getRiskNote returns Optional

// filter: keep only if predicate matches
Optional<Trade> settled = maybeTrade.filter(Trade::isSettled);

// stream (Java 9): Optional → Stream (0 or 1 element)
Stream<Trade> stream = maybeTrade.stream();  // empty() → Stream.empty(), present → Stream.of(v)
```

**Before vs After Optional:**

```java
// (Avoid) BEFORE: null-based (caller must remember to check)
Trade trade = findTrade("TRD-999");
if (trade != null) {                    // forget this → NPE!
    BigDecimal amount = trade.getAmount();
    if (amount != null) {                // nested null check!
        log.info("Amount: {}", amount);
    }
}

// (Recommended) AFTER: Optional-based (type forces handling)
findTradeOptional("TRD-999")
    .map(Trade::getAmount)               // Optional<BigDecimal> — null-safe!
    .ifPresent(amount -> log.info("Amount: {}", amount));
// No null check. No NPE. Type system guides the caller.
```

